description:
Observed 2026-10-30: diskm volume status scratch reports alarms=[scratch_capacity_unavailable] while /Volumes/diskm-scratch is mounted, active and healthy (200 GiB quota, 60-80% used).

Cause: capacity_fit reserves the FULL quota (200 GiB) + vm_reserve 40 GiB + alarm_floor 20 GiB + other_volume_allocations (~669 GiB) against a 926 GiB container = 929 GiB > 926 GiB, so fits=false and max_quota_gb_that_fits=197. The fit check therefore alarms on a configuration that is provisioned and working, which trains operators to ignore the alarm.

Acceptance:
- a mounted, active, correctly-sized scratch volume no longer reports scratch_capacity_unavailable;
- the fit formula either compares against the real container ceiling with the quota treated as a ceiling rather than an allocation, or is documented as a provisioning check only (separate command/exit path);
- test: a volume at 200 GiB quota on a 926 GiB container with 669 GiB of other volumes reports OK when mounted+active, and still alarms when the container genuinely cannot hold the declared quota.
